$DATUM 1-Hydroxyhomoadamantan-4,5-dione (3) A mixture of hydroxyketone 2 (3.6 g,
20 mmol), SeO2 (2.23 g, 20 mmol) dioxane (11 mL), and water (0.5 mL) was
stirred at 100-110°C for 3h, then cooled to room temperature, filtered
and filtrate was evaporated in vacuo to dryness to give diketone 3 (3.88
g, 100%) as yellow crystals (> 95% pure by GLC, capillary column DB-210,
200°C). An analytical sample of 3 was obtained by crystallization from
hexane/CH2Cl2; 1-Hydroxyhomoadamantan-4,5-dione (3), yield 3.88 g, 100%.
m.p. = 179-180°C. IR (KBr) cm-1 : 3460 (s), 2920 (s), 2860 (m), 1710 (s),
1450 (m), 1410 (w), 1350 (w), 1300 (w), 1100 (m), 1060 (m), 1040 (s),
1000 (m), 930 (w), 860 (w). 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ: 1.74-2.11 (m, 10H), 2.26
(br.s, 1H), 2.52 (br.s, 1H), 3.05 (br.s, 2H). 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ: 30.71
(d, 1C), 31.52 (t, 2C), 39.55 (d, 2C), 41.89 (t, 1C), 45.16 (t, 2C),
67.00 (s, 1C), 201.38 (s, 2C). Anal. Calcd. for C11H14O3 (194.23): C,
68.02; H, 7.27. Found: C, 67.91; H, 7.38.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
