$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of arylglyoxals 1 under microwave irradiation; General
Procedure. The appropriate acetophenone (2 mmol) and SeO2 (3 mmol) were
dissolved in CH2Cl2 (7 mL). Silica gel (2 g) was added and stirred
vigorously. After 5 min, the solvent was removed under vacuum and the dry
powder was irradiated in a domestic microwave oven for 7-10 min at 450 W.
After the completion of the reaction, the product was extracted with
CH2Cl2 (3 x 15 mL) and washed with excess of water to remove unreacted
SeO2. The CH2Cl2 extract after drying over anhyd Na2SO4 and removal under
reduced pressure gave aryglyoxal 1. Compound 1a, yield 68-81%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM silica gel used, Microwave
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Microwave assisted synthesis of 1,5-disubstituted hydantoins and
thiohydantoins under solvent-free conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Paul, Satya; Gupta, Mukta; Gupta, Rajive; Loupy, Andre
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2002), (1), 75-78

