$DATUM Synthesis of Ethanedione Derivatives 2a-q (General Procedure). Selenium
dioxide (0.15 mol) was added to the solution of ethanone derivative (0.1
mol) in DMSO (15 ml) and irradiated in the microwave oven for the
specified time as given in Table 1. The hot mixture was filtered to
remove the selenium metal and the filtrate was poured over crushed ice.
The resulting precipitate was filtered, dried, and recrystallized from
methanol. The ethanedione derivative. The results are summarized in Table
1. Compound: 2a; Yield: 77 % as oil.
