$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-(4-methoxyphenyl)-2-(3-nitrophenyl) ethane-1,2-dione (4) Following the
literature procedure5, to a suspension of 0.8 g (2.95 mmol) of (2) in
15ml of 70% acetic acid, 0.49 g (4.42 mmol) of selenium dioxide was
added. The mixture was refluxed overnight. After cooling to rt, the
mixture was filtered through celiteto separate the Se metal. The filtrate
was poured into thrice its volume of water and then extracted with ethyl
acetate. The organic layer was washed with water, saturated Na2CO3
solution, brine respectively and then subjected to column chromatography.
0.82 g (2.87 mmol, 97%) of (3); yellow solid. mp 120-122°C; IR (Neat,
cm-1 ) νmax: 3461, 2922, 2851, 1718, 1676, 1648, 1600, 1528, 1427, 1353,
1312, 1265, 1211, 1169, 1028, 911,720, 697; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3 ):
δppm) 8.81 (1H,s), 8.52-8.50(1H, d, J 8.0 Hz), 8.34-8.32 (1H, d, J 8.0
Hz), 8.02-8.00 (2H, d, J 8.0 Hz), 7.76-7.72 (1H, t, J 8.0 Hz), 7.04-7.02
(2H,d, J 8.0 Hz), 3.93 (3H,s) ; 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3 ): δppm) 191.6,
191.0, 165.4, 148.5, 135.2, 134.5, 132.6, 130.1, 128.6, 125.4, 124.6,
114.5, 55.7 ; HRMS m/z for (C15H11NO5+Na), calcd: 308.0637; found:
308.0649.
