$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of Ethanedione Derivatives 2a-q
(General Procedure). Selenium dioxide (0.15 mol) was added to the
solution of ethanone derivative (0.1 mol) in DMSO (15 ml) and irradiated
in the microwave oven for the specified time as given in Table 1. The hot
mixture was filtered to remove the selenium metal and the filtrate was
poured over crushed ice. The resulting precipitate was filtered, dried,
and recrystallized from methanol. The ethanedione derivative. The results
are summarized in Table 1. Compound: 2p; Yield: 94 %. M.p: 101-103°C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
