$DATUM 123-91-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Reaction of isosteviol Ia with selenium dioxide in a dioxane-acetic
anhydride mixture. A solution of 0.3 g (0.9 mmol) of isosteviol Ia and
0.5 g (4.5 mmol) of selenium dioxide was heated in a mixture of 12 ml of
dioxane and 3 ml of acetic anhydride for 10 h at the bath temperature
120°C. The reaction mixture was processed by analogy with the preceeding
experiment. After recrystallization from the benzene diketone IIa was
isolated. Yield 0.28 g (93%). 15,16-dioxo-ent-beyeran-19-oic acid (IIa).
Orange crystals. mp 305-308°C, [α]D 20 -182.5 (c 0.58, CHCl3). IR
spectrum, ν, cm-1: 1753 (С15=О), 1732 (С16=О), 1692 (СООН), 1252, 1029,
954, 930. 1Н NMR spectrum, δ , ppm (J, Hz): 0.66-2.47 m (27Н, entbeyeran
framework), 0.66 s (3Н, С20Н3), 1.14 s (3Н, С17Н3), 1.26 s (3Н, С18Н3),
2.19 d (1Н, J 14), 2.36- 2.47 m (1Н). The EI mass spectrum, m/z: [M]+
332. Found, %: С 71.72; Н 9.18. С20Н28О4. Calculated, %: С 72.25; Н 8.51.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, alternatively reaction carried out using acetic anhydride
as solvent decreased yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Reaction of isosteviol diterpenoid with selenium dioxide
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kovylyaeva, G. I.; Sharipova, R. R.; Strobykina, I. Yu.; Militsina, O.
I.; Musin, R. Z.; Beskrovnyi, D. V.; Gubaidullin, A. T.; Al'fonsov, V.
A.; Kataev, V. E.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
