$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4,5-Protoadamantanedione (2): A mixture of 4-protoadamantanone (1; 1.50
g, 10 mmol), selenium dioxide (1.22 g,11 mmol), and 90% aqueous dioxan (5
ml) is stirred at 90°C for 24 h. After cooling, ether (25 ml) is added,
the resulting mixture is filtered, washed with water (3 × 10 ml), and
dried. Evaporation of the solvent at room temperature leaves the crude
product, which is recrystallized from n-hexane. bright yellow diketone 2;
yield: 1.51 g (92%). m.p. 230-233 °C. C10H12O2 (164.2), calc. C 73.14, H
7.37, found C 72.92, H 7.45, M.S.: m/e (rel. intensity) = 164 (M+, 31);
136 (15); 118 (10); 108 (11); 107 (17); 92 (18); 80 (36); 79 (100); 67
(41); 66 (82); 58 (71). I.R. (KBr): ν = 2925; 2860; 1728; 1460; 1447;
1260; 1113; 1035; 1012; 852 cm-1. 1H-N.M.R. (CCl4): δ = 3.2-1.4 ppm
(complex m, maxima at 1.93 and 1.80 ppm). 13C-N.M.R. (CDCl3): δ=203.5;
198.8; 47.4; 46.3; 40.5; 37.4; 37.0; 36.8; 36.5; 29.6 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A facile route to 2-noradamantanone via 4-protoadamantanone
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Majerski, Zdenko; Sarac-Arneri, Ruza; Skare, Danko; Loncar, Bozo
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (1980), (1), 74-5

