$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl-3β-acetoxy-21,22-dioxo[3α-3H]lup-18-en-28-oate (25). Ketone 22 (28
mCi, 18 μmol) was dissolved in a mixture of 1,4-dioxane (120 μL), acetic
acid (60 μL), acetic anhydride (8 μL) and selenium dioxide (15 mg, 133
μmol) was added. The mixture was stirred and heated to reflux under argon
atmosphere for 3 h. The reaction was monitored by TLC in
toluene/diethylether (5:1). The reaction was diluted with ethyl acetate
(2 mL) and filtered over silica gel (500 mg). Organic layer was washed
with water and solvents were evaporated under vacuum. Preparative TLC in
toluene/ diethylether (5:1). Radiochemical yield(25 mCi, 89 %).
radio-RP-HPLC in MeOH/H2O (6:4), tr 12.0 min; 1H NMR (B 300 MHz): δ 0.85
s, 3H; 0.86 s, 3H; 0.92 s, 3H; 0.97 s, 3H; 1.06 s, 3H; 1.26 d, 3H (J =
4.4); 1.29 d, 3H (J = 4.4); (7 × CH3); 2.05 s, 3H (OAc); 3.48 s, 3H
(OCH3); 4.20 septet, 1H (∑J = 4.4, H-20). 3H NMR (B 300 MHz): δ 4.47 s,
(3H-3α).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM radiochemical (yield determined), controlled oxidation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of selectively deuterated and tritiated lupane derivatives with
cytotoxic activity
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Vlk, Martin; Urban, Milan; Elbert, Tomas; Sarek, Jan
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Radioanalytical and Nuclear Chemistry (2013), 298(2),
1149-1157

