$DATUM Compound 4. A solution of 360 mg (0.46 mmol) of 7, 150 mg (1.35 mmol) of
selenium dioxide and 0.5 mL of water in 120 mL of degassed benzene was
refluxed for 18 h. The volumn of the solution was evaporated to 30 mL and
submitted to column chromatography (SiO2, toluene to toluene/ethyl
acetate-5:1) to give 305 mg (83%) of 4 as a brown solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl2-CDCl2) δ (ppm) 7.03 (s, 2H); FT-IR (KBr) ν (cm-1) 2922 w, 1735 s,
1622 w, 1426 m, 1088 s, 1038 s, 729 m, 523 s; HRMS calcd for C64H2O2
(M+): 802.0055, found: 802.0030.
