$DATUM 7446-08-4
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 68-12-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: tert-butyl
5-((14Z)-1-(5-formyl-3,4-dihydro-4,4-dimethylpyrrol-2-
ylidene)ethyl)-3,4-dimethyl-1H-pyrrole-2-carboxylate (12a). A solution of
21a (717 mg, 2.17 mmol) in DMF (20 mL) and pyridine (210 μL, 2.60 mmol)
was treated with SeO2 (289 mg, 2.60 mmol) and stirred at rt for 5 h. The
reaction was then heated to 80°C for 15 min. The reaction mixture was
cooled to rt, filtered, and poured into water. The solution was extracted
with CH2Cl2 (3 × 10 mL), and the combined organic extracts were washed
sequentially with saturated aq NaHCO3 and brine, dried over Na2SO4,
filtered, and concentrated. The resulting oil was purified by flash
chromatography (silica gel, EtOAc:hexanes = 3:7) to give 12a (483 mg,
65%) as an orange crystalline solid. tert-butyl
5-((14Z)-(5-formyl-3,4-dihydro-4,4-dimethylpyrrol-2-ylidene)-
(phenyl)methyl)-3,4-dimethyl-1H-pyrrole-2-carboxylate (12b). Following
the procedure outlined for 12a, reaction of 21b (1.79 g, 4.56 mmol) with
SeO2 (607 mg, 5.47 mmol) in DMF (53 mL) and pyridine (440 μL, 5.47 mmol)
gave 12b (1.49 g, 81%) as an orange crystalline solid. mp 162.0-162.6°C.
R f (1:4 EtOAc/hexanes) 0.52; IR(thin film)1687, 1442, 1170 cm-1; 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.24 (s, 3H), 1.30 (s, 6H), 1.61 (s, 9H), 2.20 (s,
3H), 2.49 (s, 2H), 7.25-7.27 (m, 2H), 7.42-7.44 (m, 3H), 9.98 (s, 1H),
11.26 (br s, 1H) ; 13C NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 10.3, 10.5, 25.9, 28.6,
28.7, 45.9, 46.7, 80.7, 122.3, 123.7, 127.2, 128.2, 129.1, 129.2, 129.9,
131.1, 139.2, 150. 6, 161.0, 177.5, 190.4. Anal. Calcd for C25H30N2O3: C,
73.96; H, 7.44; N, 6.89; O, 11.71. Found: C, 73.68; H, 7.58; N, 6.85.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Toward a General Synthesis of Chlorins
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM O'Neal, William G.; Jacobi, Peter A.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2008), 130(3), 1102-1108

