$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 26 Method A: Oxidation of 2a Using Selenium Dioxide A
solution of compound 1a (1g) selenium dioxide (0.5 g) in dioxane (25 ml)
and water (2 ml) was refluxed with stirring for 3h. The reaction mixture
was then cooled, poured into ice- cooled water (100 ml), and the
resultant solid product was filtered off, washed with water and
recrystallized from ethanol-dioxane (2:1). Compound 26 as yellow
crystals. mp 210 °C; mol. formula (mol. weight): C19H13N3O3S (363.39). IR
(cm-1): 1680 (S-C=O), 1640 (N-C=O), 1610 (C=C) and 1550 (strong, Ar). 1H
NMR (DMSO-d6) δ (ppm): 1.21(s, 3H, CH3), 7.23-8.21 (m, 10H, Ar-H). CH3:
16.9. CH: 120.4, 125.7, 126.4, 127.3, 128.9, 129.4. Cq: 109.3, 138.3,
149.1, 152.1, 155.6, 167.1, 187.7. M.S. (%): M+: 363 (35.3), 286 (32),
209 (20), 194 (43), 162 (15.4).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternate prepn. also described
