$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5-Trifluorobutoxyninhydrin 3f. 6f (1.8 g, 6.97 mmol) was added to a
suspension of selenium dioxide (3.87 g, 34.8 mmol) in dioxane (10 mL).
The suspension was then stirred for 4 h to reflux under an argon
atmosphere and filtered, and the solvents were evaporated. The residue
was poured into dichloromethane (30 mL) into which the unreacted SeO2
precipitated. The SeO2 was filtered off and the filtrate evaporated to
dryness. The residue was purified by column chromatography over silica
gel eluted with CH2Cl2/ AcOEt (3:1) to give 3f (1.56 g, 74%) TLC: R f
(CH2Cl2/AcOEt 7:3) 0.3
