$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A mixture of dioxane (7 mL) and H2O (0.3 mL) and selenium dioxide (855
mg, 7.7 mmol) was heated at 50-55 °C, with stirring, until the selenium
dioxide dissolved, and then 4-benzyloxy-3,3-dimethyl-butan-2-one (1.44 g,
7 mmol) was added in one pot. Refluxing and vigorous stirring were
continued for 18 h, after which the reaction mixture was cooled and the
precipitated selenium was removed by filtration. The yellow filtrate was
concentrated and purified by short flash chromatography (SiO2: 20% EtOA
in hexanes) followed by Kugelrohr distillation to give the glyoxal 2 in
75% yield as a yellow oil. 2, yield 75% 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.22
(s, 1H), 7.35-7.22 (m, 5H), 4.43 (s, 2H), 3.67 (s, 2H), 1.25 (s, 6H) 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 203.0, 188.9, 138.1, 128.9, 128.2, 128.0, 76.5,
73.8, 47.3, 22.1 HRMS calcd for C13H16O3 [M] 220.1099, found 220.1105
FTIR (neat) 3429, 2975, 2867, 1708, 1454, 1364, 1266, 1207, 1097, 738,
698 cm-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Enantioselective Reductive Coupling of Alkynes and α-Keto Aldehydes via
Rhodium-Catalyzed Hydrogenation: An Approach to Bryostatin Substructures
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cho, Chang-Woo; Krische, Michael J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2006), 8(5), 891-894

